# AI Tools (bootloader — spec in `docs/modules/ai-tools.md`; Explain chat in `docs/modules/dashboard.md`)

## Invariants
- `AI_TOOLS_ENABLED` gates every AI route (400) except `POST .../assets/generate-img` (Word render, no LLM; only the UI hides it). Image ops need `supports_vision`; `_ai_load_endpoint*` rejects text-only endpoints even when named.
- Default endpoint per feature: `llm_client.resolve_default_endpoint('<FEATURE>_DEFAULT_LLM')` → named enabled endpoint → first enabled by `sort_order, name` → `None`. `endpoint_id` blank/`0` falls back to the setting. `SMART_IMPORT_DEFAULT_LLM` is text-only (`vision_only=False`).
- Batch routes intersect `question_ids` with `get_user_admin_subjects()`; endpoint CRUD / test / duplicate / chat are super-admin only.
- Parallel only when `parallel=1` **and** `kind=='cloud'` **and** `max_concurrency>1` (`_ai_parallel` → `app/parallel.run_parallel`). Workers are pure; all counters and SSE emission happen on the consumer thread; each parallel `iter_check` worker owns a short-lived `_LazyWord`.
- Check-state is **per format**: `check_slot_format` writes only that format's rows (IMG parts share one state). `check_raw` (≤ 32 000 chars) is always stored by AI checks and nulled by manual/batch edits. Rollups ignore ENO/CHO. `check_answer_text` never persists. Per-slot Quick Check defaults `recheck=true`; batch defaults `recheck=0`.
- Reasoning: endpoint `off` wins; blank inherits `LLM_REASONING_EFFORT_DEFAULT` / `LLM_REASONING_SUMMARY_DEFAULT`. Claude models (`_is_claude_model`) get `thinking:{type:adaptive}` + `output_config.effort`, never top-level `reasoning` (Poe → deprecated `thinking.type.enabled`).
- Responses API streaming: consume `*.delta` events only; never harvest `response.output_item.done` (duplicates text). `resp.encoding='utf-8'` is forced (LM Studio / Ollama mojibake).
- `service_tier` for single calls, `service_tier_batch` only when transient `config._batch` is set; blank tiers are omitted.
- API keys: Fernet key = SHA-256(`LLM_KEY_SECRET` or `SECRET_KEY`). Rotating either silently invalidates `api_key_enc` (falls back to `.env` `LLM_API_KEY`). Plaintext never reaches the browser.
- Interactive chat (Explain, endpoint console) uses `LLM_CHAT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` (0 = endpoint timeout); batch ops use the endpoint's `timeout_seconds`.

## Routes (verify before use)
- Batch SSE under `/admin/questions/ai/*` (`check`, `generate-md`, `solve-generate`, `solve-check`, `auto-tag`, `cancel`, `endpoints`); per-slot sync under `/admin/questions/<qid>/assets/ai/*` and `.../ai/answer-text`, `.../ai/suggest-tags`; verify via `set_question_verified`; endpoints under `/admin/llm-endpoints[/data|/save|/<cid>/test|...]`.
- `suggest-tags` returns `{success, suggestions, display, unmatched, fields, model}`; `raw` only on parse failure.

## Gotchas
- New LLM feature = prompt key in `ai_prompts.PROMPTS_REGISTRY` + worker in `ai_tools.py` + `<FEATURE>_DEFAULT_LLM` setting + docs (`ai-tools.md`, `ai-prompts.md`, `core/06`).
- Images are downscaled to `LLM_IMAGE_MAX_DIM` before sending; MD/DOC slots are rendered to images first.
- Cancel registry is in-process; a multi-worker deployment would break it.
